#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:United States of America}}
#: {{ux|en|Mexico and Canada border the '''United States of America'''.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|date=November 15, 1777
|origyear=1776
|title=w:Articles of Confederation and Perpetual Union
|location=Philadelphia
|publisher=w:Second Continental Congress
|oclc=1199170160
|page=1
|pageurl=https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Articles_of_Confederation_1-5.jpg
|text=Whereas the Delegates of the '''United States of America''' in Congreſs assembled did on the 15th day of November in the Year of our Lord One Thousand Seven Hundred and Seventy seven, and in the Second Year of the Independence of America agree to certain articles of Confederation and perpetual Union between the states of Newhampſhire, Maſsachusetts-bay, Rhodeiſland and Providence Plantations, Connecticut, New York, New Jersey, Pennsylvania, Delaware, Maryland, Virginia, North Carolina, South Carolina and Georgia in the Words following, viz.{{...}}<br>ARTICLE I. The Stile of this confederacy shall be "The '''United States of America'''."}}
#* {{quote-av
|en
|date=April 28, 1942
|author=w:Franklin Roosevelt
|title={{w|Fireside Chat}} 21: On Sacrifice
|url=https://millercenter.org/the-presidency/presidential-speeches/april-28-1942-fireside-chat-21-sacrifice
|publisher=w:Miller Center
|time=30:57
|text=As we here at home contemplate our own duties, our own responsibilities, let us think and think hard of the example which is being set for us by our fighting men. Our soldiers and sailors are members of well disciplined units. But they are still and forever individuals -- free individuals. They are farmers, and workers, businessmen, professional men, artists, clerks. They are the '''United States of America'''. That is why they fight. We too are the '''United States of America'''. That is why we must work and sacrifice. It is for them. It is for us. It is for victory.}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=January 30, 2023
|author=w:Zolan Kanno-Youngs; Mark Walker
|quotee=w:Joe Biden
|title=Biden Visits Decrepit Rail Tunnel to Promote $1 Trillion Infrastructure Law
|journal=w:The New York Times
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230130232045/https://www.nytimes.com/2023/01/30/us/politics/biden-infrastructure-tunnel-baltimore.html
|issn=0362-4331
|oclc=1645522
|section=Politics
|url2=https://archive.is/uW1Ja
|text=“The structure is deteriorating. The roof was leaking. The floor is sinking,” Mr. Biden said in a speech in front of the tunnel, the oldest in the Northeast, where the crowd included dozens of union workers. “This is the '''United States of America''', for God’s sake. We know better than that.”}}

